Good point 👍 — ports are **very important**, especially for interviews and DevOps work.
Here is a **clear + standard port mapping** for **Web, App, and Database servers**.

---

## 1️⃣ Web Server Ports 🌐

### Common Ports

| Port    | Protocol | Use                          |
| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------- |
| **80**  | HTTP     | Default web traffic          |
| **443** | HTTPS    | Secure web traffic (SSL/TLS) |

### Examples

* **Nginx / Apache / IIS**

```
http://example.com      → Port 80
https://example.com     → Port 443
```

✅ These ports are **publicly accessible**

---

## 2️⃣ Application Server Ports ⚙️

Application servers usually run on **internal ports** (not exposed directly).

### Common App Server Ports

| Technology                      | Port        |
| ------------------------------- | ----------- |
| **Node.js (Express)**           | 3000        |
| **Spring Boot**                 | 8080        |
| **Tomcat**                      | 8080 / 8443 |
| **Laravel (php artisan serve)** | 8000        |
| **Django**                      | 8000        |
| **Flask**                       | 5000        |
| **PHP-FPM**                     | 9000        |

### Example Flow

```
Client → 80/443 (Web Server)
Web Server → 8080 / 3000 / 9000 (App Server)
```

⚠️ App server ports are usually **blocked from public access**

---

## 3️⃣ Database Server Ports 🗄️

### Common Database Ports

| Database            | Default Port |
| ------------------- | ------------ |
| **MySQL / MariaDB** | 3306         |
| **PostgreSQL**      | 5432         |
| **MongoDB**         | 27017        |
| **Oracle**          | 1521         |
| **SQL Server**      | 1433         |
| **Redis**           | 6379         |
| **Elasticsearch**   | 9200         |

🚫 Database ports should be **private only**

---

## 🔁 Complete Port Flow (3-Tier Architecture)

```
Internet User
   ↓
Web Server  : 80 / 443
   ↓
App Server  : 8080 / 3000 / 9000
   ↓
DB Server   : 3306 / 5432
```

---

## 🧠 Real Laravel Production Example

| Layer | Software | Port     |
| ----- | -------- | -------- |
| Web   | Nginx    | 80 / 443 |
| App   | PHP-FPM  | 9000     |
| DB    | MySQL    | 3306     |

```
User → Nginx(80/443) → PHP-FPM(9000) → MySQL(3306)
```

---

## 🎯 Interview Quick Answer

> **Web Server:** 80, 443
> **Application Server:** 3000, 8080, 8000, 9000 (internal)
> **Database Server:** 3306, 5432, 27017 (private)

